शूर् (also written सूर्) cl. 4. Ā. (Dhātup. xxvi, 48) शूर्यते, to hurt, injure, kill (only in pf. शुशूरे, ‘he cut off [the head]’, Śiś. xix, 108);
to be or make firm, Dhātup.; ib.;
 cl. 10. Ā. to be powerful or valiant (in this sense rather Nom. fr. next), Dhātup. xxxv, 48.

शूर् (also written सूर्) cl. 4. Ā. (Dhātup. xxvi, 48) शूर्यते, to hurt, injure, kill (only in pf. शुशूरे, ‘he cut off [the head]’, Śiś. xix, 108);
to be or make firm, Dhātup.; ib.;
 cl. 10. Ā. to be powerful or valiant (in this sense rather Nom. fr. next), Dhātup. xxxv, 48.

सुर् (rather Nom. fr. सुर below) cl. 6. P. सुरति, to rule, possess supreme or superhuman power, Dhātup. xxviii, 50;
to shine, ib.;
 cl. 10. P. सुरयति, to find fault (v.l. for स्वर्), xxxv, 11.

सूर्मि or सूर्मी॑, f. (rather fr. √ सृ than fr. सु + ऊर्मि; also written शूर्मि and शूर्मी) a pipe for conveying water, RV.; ŚBr.;
 a kind of tube serving as a candlestick, RV.; TS.; Kāṭh.;
 a metal image, W.;
 a hollow metal column made red-hot for burning criminals (esp. adulterers) to death, Gaut.; Mn. &c.

